A narrative is your field journal. Use it to record observations, decisions,
and other context that may not fit in a specimen or event record.

## Creating a narrative

{% steps %}

1. Open the Narrative page {% ref id="A" /%} from the navigation bar.
2. Select `+` or `Create narrative` {% ref id="B" /%}.
3. Enter the `Date` {% ref id="C" /%} and, optionally, the `Time`.
4. Select a `Site` {% ref id="D" /%}. The site name is displayed automatically from the site's
   locality information.

    {% aside type="note" %}
    Create at least one site on the [Sites page](/en/usages/sites) before
    selecting a site for a narrative.
    {% /aside %}

5. Select the `Writer` {% ref id="E" /%} from the personnel assigned to the project.
6. Enter the narrative text {% ref id="F" /%}.

{% /steps %}

Narrative fields persist automatically. Leave the entry and reopen it to confirm the date, writer, site, and text before moving on.

The date and time are stored separately. If you enter a time without a date,
NAHPU uses the current date.

## Writing and previewing text

Narrative text supports Markdown. Use the `Preview` and `Edit` {% ref id="I" /%} controls above
the text field to switch between writing and rendered views.

### Markdown cheat sheet

You do not need Markdown to write a narrative. Plain text works, and the
formatting below is there when a long entry is easier to read with structure.

| What you want | What you type | What you get |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Bold | `**set before dusk**` | **set before dusk** |
| Italic | `_Bunomys penitus_` | _Bunomys penitus_ |
| Strikethrough | `~~12 traps~~` | ~~12 traps~~ |
| Heading | `## Morning check` | a section heading |
| Bullet list | `- checked line 1` | a bulleted item |
| Numbered list | `1. checked line 1` | a numbered item |
| Checklist | `- [ ] rebait traps` | a checkbox item |
| Quote | `> guide reported rain` | an indented quote block |
| Code or a fixed-width value | `` `GPHH-L1` `` | `GPHH-L1` |
| Link | `[GBIF](https://gbif.org)` | [GBIF](https://gbif.org) |

Three more rules cover most of the rest:

- Leave a blank line between paragraphs. A single line break inside a
  paragraph is treated as a space.
- Indent by four spaces to nest a list item under another one.
- Write `---` on its own line for a horizontal rule between sections of a long
  day.

Switch to `Preview` to confirm the entry reads the way you intended before you
move on. Markdown is stored as you typed it, so exports and backups keep the
raw text.

## Adding media

Attach media to a narrative from the camera, device gallery, or file picker.
Narrative media is included when the project is transferred and can also be
included in exports where narrative media is selected.

## Searching and managing narratives

Use the search button {% ref id="G" /%} in the Narrative app bar to filter narrative entries.
Use the page controls {% ref id="H" /%} to move between entries. The menu for the selected entry
provides these deletion actions:

- **Delete narrative** - Delete the selected narrative and its associated
  media.
- **Delete all narrative** - Delete every narrative in the active project.

Deletion is permanent. Export or back up the project first if the entries may
be needed later.
